course: dictionary
lesson: 13674
title: Inhabitants: who lives here?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inhabitant is a person or animal that lives in a place. Look for the word inhabitant when a text tells you who or what lives somewhere. «The town has 5,000 inhabitants» means 5,000 people live in the town.
explain: The word can also mean an animal that lives in a habitat, which is the place where it naturally lives. «The inhabitants of the pond are frogs, newts and snails» tells you the animals that live in the pond.
explain: Inhabitant is a noun, and the plural is inhabitants. To check your meaning, swap in the words "people who live in" or "animals that live in". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: An inhabitant is a person who lives in a place, such as a town, island or country.
fact: An inhabitant can also be an animal that lives in a particular habitat.
fact: «The town has 5,000 inhabitants» means 5,000 people live in the town.
fact: «The inhabitants of the pond» means the animals that live in the pond.
fact: Inhabitant is a noun. Its plural is inhabitants.
exercise: «The town has 5,000 inhabitants.» What does inhabitants mean here? | Visitors who stay for one night | Shops and offices | *People who live in the town | Plants growing in the town parks
exercise: «The inhabitants of the pond are frogs, newts and snails.» What are the inhabitants of the pond? | Water and weeds in the pond | Ducks who stop by for lunch | *Animals that live in the pond | Stones on the bottom of the pond
exercise: «The island's inhabitants wave to every boat.» Find and copy the word that tells you who lives on the island. | wave | *inhabitants | island | boat
test: Ella says, «Each inhabitant of the village got a letter.» What is an inhabitant? | *A person who lives in the village | A stranger passing through the village | A letter carrier | A village shop
test: Sam says wolves are inhabitants of the forest. Is he right? | No, wolves only visit the forest | Yes, but only for one day | No, only people can be inhabitants | *Yes, an inhabitant can be an animal that lives in a habitat
exam: «The island has 300 inhabitants, and most of them fish for a living.» What does inhabitants mean? | Tourists with cameras | Fish that swim near the island | *People who live on the island | Boats that visit each week
